{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-12-11","kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：圆柱与圆锥","englishTitle":"Cones and cylinders which are of the same height are to one another as their bases.","book":12,"number":11,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:12.prop.11","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:12.prop.11/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":11,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","contentId":"euclid-12-11","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"65801540c1882cac763cb561c774096a84b5144e110c054f6c9fa97975cb378b","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-12-11.statement","euclid-12-11.construction.1","euclid-12-11.proof.1","euclid-12-11.proof.2","euclid-12-11.construction.2","euclid-12-11.construction.3","euclid-12-11.construction.4","euclid-12-11.proof.3","euclid-12-11.proof.4","euclid-12-11.proof.5","euclid-12-11.construction.5","euclid-12-11.construction.6","euclid-12-11.proof.6","euclid-12-11.proof.7","euclid-12-11.proof.8","euclid-12-11.proof.9","euclid-12-11.proof.10","euclid-12-11.proof.11","euclid-12-11.proof.12","euclid-12-11.proof.13","euclid-12-11.proof.14","euclid-12-11.proof.15","euclid-12-11.proof.16","euclid-12-11.proof.17","euclid-12-11.proof.18","euclid-12-11.proof.19","euclid-12-11.conclusion","euclid-12-11.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-12-11.statement","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"f9338517067070f3909af55ccfd32575c00a57c85bc7fe6f26d777193234d29c","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Cones and cylinders which are of the same height are to one another as their bases."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"高度和底边一样的锥形和圆筒是相互的"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"e54a18a05da74d2e6fa9f7251a48dfcbee5d1a59cccfb5fe7d4fdaabd99aab96","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let there be cones and cylinders of the same height, let the circles ABCD, EFGH be their bases, KL, MN their axes and AC, EG the diameters of their bases; I say that, as the circle ABCD is to the circle EFGH, so is the cone AL to the cone EN."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"允许有同一高度的锥形和圆锥体,让ABCD,EFGH圈成为它们的底边,KL,MN轴,AC,ABCD直径是它们的底边;我说,ABCD圆与圆圆EFGH的比等于锥形AL对锥体EN的比。（相关点与线段：EG）"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"71a0132e00bc62485b711bc67ae708ec39b6eeb1d3d47c4eca7ca94c0a278d86","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, if not, then, as the circle ABCD is to the circle EFGH, so will the cone AL be either to some solid less than the cone EN or to a greater."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果不是,那么,ABCD圆是EFGH圆,AL锥体要么是比EN锥体更固态的,要么更大。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c10f71a14f7dd53af1f2caf6a85b8a60b0f777cc987f1dfd026a105cc7da38b4","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"First, let it be in that ratio to a less solid O, and let the solid X be equal to that by which the solid O is less than the cone EN; therefore the cone EN is equal to the solids O, X."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"首先,让它以较不固体的O比X等于O比锥体小的X;因此,EN等于O和X。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.construction.2","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":4,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"8ddd817828441d4146f5ef1edf67cfd7d48e5596dedd948ac4eb9eef48b8c0a7","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let the square EFGH be inscribed in the circle EFGH; therefore the square is greater than the half of the circle."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让正方形 EFGH在EFGH圆内标注,因此正方形大于该圆的一半。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.construction.3","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":5,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"f0d40b508644a5a2b0ba0eb408faba4e583300d13d1411b43f9b96a565f27f7a","citations":["euclid-12-6"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let there be set up from the square EFGH a pyramid of equal height with the cone; therefore the pyramid so set up is greater than the half of the cone, inasmuch as, if we circumscribe a square about the circle, and set up from it a pyramid of equal height with the cone, the inscribed pyramid is half of the circumscribed pyramid, for they are to one another as their bases, [[XII. 6](/principles/euclid-12-6)] while the cone is less than the circumscribed pyramid."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"由正方形 EFGH金字塔建立, 与锥体一样高, 因此金字塔的建立大于锥体的一半, 因为如果我们将圆圈的界限限定为正方形, 并从中建立一座金字塔, 与锥体一样高, 被刻着的金字塔是被限制的金字塔的一半, 因为金字塔是彼此的底边, 而锥体的界限比被限定的金字塔小。 [[XII. 6](/principles/euclid-12-6)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.construction.4","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":6,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"8cb24acf405be97df08763eb307aeb5186f66e51cca77d2624f950b103834c9a","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let the circumferences EF, FG, GH, HE be bisected at the points P, Q, R, S, and let HP, PE, EQ, QF, FR, RG, GS, SH be joined."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让EF、FG、GH、HE环绕线在P、Q、R、S点两分为两部分,让HP、PE、EQ、QF、FR、RG、GS、SH环绕线连接。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":7,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"7bb9c107eb07a9e135e6197f40b8371f238b1b06c1d38f2fce70f53b421ed80f","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore each of the triangles HPE, EQF, FRG, GSH is greater than the half of that segment of the circle which is about it."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,HPE、EQF、FRG、GSH三角形的每一个三角形都大于圆圈的这一段的一半。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":8,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"e5c968ed16ff2766790e82eaeb0b7d5cb0cf65de1d9843d21cc7355bcb86f745","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"On each of the triangles HPE, EQF, FRG, GSH let there be set up a pyramid of equal height with the cone; therefore, also, each of the pyramids so set up is greater than the half of that segment of the cone which is about it."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"三角形HPE,EQF,FRG,GSH 允许在每一个三角形上建立一个与锥形相等的金字塔;因此,如此建立的金字塔每个金字塔都大于锥形中一半的金字塔。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":9,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c363ba81221e609bbe47b76e68c4354371a18afa1e361e291c1804a6b5f224d0","citations":["euclid-10-1"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Thus, bisecting the circumferences which are left, joining straight lines, setting up on each of the triangles pyramids of equal height with the cone, and doing this continually, we shall leave some segments of the cone which will be less than the solid X. [[X. 1](/principles/euclid-10-1)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,在将剩下的圆形两分开,连接直线,在每根三角形上建立与锥体相等的金字塔,并且不断这样做,我们将留下一些小于X固体的锥体部分。 [[X. 1](/principles/euclid-10-1)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.construction.5","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":10,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"e248c6975e9dd56a12efd4cfc02abadabb60f1b8d8b71f1698dbb38e7585a529","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let such be left, and let them be the segments on HP, PE, EQ, QF, FR, RG, GS, SH; therefore the remainder, the pyramid of which the polygon HPEQFRGS is the base and the height the same with that of the cone, is greater than the solid O."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"任由这些部分留下,并任由它们成为HP、PE、EQ、QF、FR、RG、GS、SH段;因此,其余部分,其中多边形个HPEQFRGS是底边,与锥体高度相同,大于O的固体。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.construction.6","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":11,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 6","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c09ccf51463c5d7b1e09a0cbb08624d7d6fb9d0cb843428872a49de0542385b6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let there also be inscribed in the circle ABCD the polygon DTAUBVCW similar and similarly situated to the polygon HPEQFRGS, and on it let a pyramid be set up of equal height with the cone AL."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"也让ABCD圈的多边形DTAUBVCW类似和类似HPEQFRGS, 并让金字塔与AL锥形同高。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.6","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":12,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 6","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"502fcba0c83cf3a3ee3ab07f5201bf983ca1416fd92ba2607a3f328947503473","citations":["euclid-12-1","euclid-12-2"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Since then, as the square on AC is to the square on EG, so is the polygon DTAUBVCW to the polygon HPEQFRGS, [[XII. 1](/principles/euclid-12-1)] while, as the square on AC is to the square on EG, so is the circle ABCD to the circle EFGH, [[XII. 2](/principles/euclid-12-2)] therefore also, as the circle ABCD is to the circle EFGH, so is the polygon DTAUBVCW to the polygon HPEQFRGS."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"从那时起,AC比正方形等于EG比多边形,多边形德国先令与多边形日本先令和EG比正方形,AC比正方形等于ABCD比EFGH,ABCD比EFGH,多边形德国先令和多边形日本先令和多边形日本先令的比。 [[XII. 1](/principles/euclid-12-1)] [[XII. 2](/principles/euclid-12-2)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.7","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":13,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 7","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"571cf1d5c736bb21fafa0fb32f551a2ad8de62b92a471f3b0559c37f66a8e88b","citations":["euclid-12-6"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But, as the circle ABCD is to the circle EFGH, so is the cone AL to the solid O, and, as the polygon DTAUBVCW is to the polygon HPEQFRGS, so is the pyramid of which the polygon DTAUBVCW is the base and the point L the vertex to the pyramid of which the polygon HPEQFRGS is the base and the point N the vertex. [[XII. 6](/principles/euclid-12-6)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但是,ABCD圆与EFGH圆之比等于AL圆与O固体之比,多边形DTAUBVCW与多边形HPEQFRGS之比等于金字塔之比,其中多边形DTAUBVCW是底边,L点是金字塔的顶部,多边形HPEQFRGS是底边,N点是顶部。 [[XII. 6](/principles/euclid-12-6)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.8","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":14,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 8","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"ae4d89453edf5fcc8e51a510c4f5b32ba24315f43ab03083e05ac1bfbe3c528a","citations":["euclid-5-11","euclid-5-16"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore also, as the cone AL is to the solid O, so is the pyramid of which the polygon DTAUBVCW is the base and the point L the vertex to the pyramid of which the polygon HPEQFRGS is the base and the point N the vertex; [[V. 11](/principles/euclid-5-11)] therefore, alternately, as the cone AL is to the pyramid in it, so is the solid O to the pyramid in the cone EN. [[V. 16](/principles/euclid-5-16)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,锥体AL对固体O的比也等于金字塔多边形和顶部L的比,其中,顶部多边形和顶部O是顶部O和顶部N;因此,锥体AL对金字塔AL的比等于锥体O对金字塔EN的比例。 [[V. 11](/principles/euclid-5-11)] [[V. 16](/principles/euclid-5-16)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.9","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":15,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 9","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"270ce1a1c01a91bd8d98f2ec3f930c6359097e71f841dc95eb94d44b259cb57d","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But the cone AL is greater than the pyramid in it; therefore the solid O is also greater than the pyramid in the cone EN."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但AL锥体大于金字塔,因此O固体也大于EN锥体金字塔。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.10","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":16,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 10","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"a65d7eecb2946bea3f50d0d5b32aa1a80f64f13b95c459b075d7903eac0a081a","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But it is also less: which is absurd."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但情况也并非如此:这是荒谬的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.11","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":17,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 11","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"522893320e9eb7f759501bd5a2ff94faa5f1c1fe904175576dd562f53afd0291","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore the cone AL is not to any solid less than the cone EN as the circle ABCD is to the circle EFGH."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,AL锥体与EN锥体的固体值不小,因为ABCD圆体与EFGH圆体的数值相同。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.12","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":18,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 12","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"a51ce1753e464b983dcc0a7a656c8a054d035499d5fedb98eb5e4b32fcefe08d","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Similarly we can prove that neither is the cone EN to any solid less than the cone AL as the circle EFGH is to the circle ABCD."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"同样,我们可以证明,EN锥体与AL锥体的固体值两者都不如,因为EFGH圆体与ABCD圆体的数值相同。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.13","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":19,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 13","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"1712cf398a0d8767a67f9d1e15011d81adf2ea1a83d8e0444ace547f6d949605","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"I say next that neither is the cone AL to any solid greater than the cone EN as the circle ABCD is to the circle EFGH."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"接下来我要说的是,AL锥体与EN锥体相比,都不是任何坚固的,因为ABCD圆体与EFGH圆体是相同的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.14","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":20,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 14","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"280bebe618c6a4ae77ebee245995f804640797ce9aaa3b303facf47ff00b1d62","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, if possible, let it be in that ratio to a greater solid O; therefore, inversely, as the circle EFGH is to the circle ABCD, so is the solid O to the cone AL."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果可能,则以O的固体为底边;因此,EFGH圆与ABCD圆之比等于O和AL锥体之比。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.15","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":21,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 15","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"326435cdcb0bde14a89dd1f7446168e56ce681146173afb63d1393d53ac04b1a","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But, as the solid O is to the cone AL, so is the cone EN to some solid less than the cone AL; therefore also, as the circle EFGH is to the circle ABCD, so is the cone EN to some solid less than the cone AL: which was proved impossible."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但是,O固体对AL锥体的比等于EN锥体对低于AL锥体的一些固体的比;因此,EFGH圆对ABCD圆体的比等于EN锥体对AL锥体对低于AL锥体的固体比,事实证明这是不可能的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.16","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":22,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 16","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"0dd4f403c793b8dc9298ee2e6365eefe59e65c379f9cb7adbf622e986ebadbe8","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore the cone AL is not to any solid greater than the cone EN as the circle ABCD is to the circle EFGH."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,AL锥体的固体值不超过EN锥体,因为ABCD圆体的固体值为EFGH圆。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.17","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":23,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 17","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"ca54c14082758664b2222622fadf7d5b6844ab8c77bd38f4bb23c307c51ef665","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But it was proved that neither is it in this ratio to a less solid; therefore, as the circle ABCD is to the circle EFGH, so is the cone AL to the cone EN."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但事实证明,两者的比例都不是比重较低;因此,ABCD圆与EFGH圆的比等于AL锥体与EN锥体的比。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.18","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":24,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 18","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"1f668712250deae846789d32abe5ab4eed74482240160fafbde6b639ff11228c","citations":["euclid-12-10"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But, as the cone is to the cone, so is the cylinder to the cylinder, for each is triple of each; [[XII. 10](/principles/euclid-12-10)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但是,锥体与锥体的比等于圆柱体与圆柱体的比,每个圆锥体的比例是三倍; [[XII. 10](/principles/euclid-12-10)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.proof.19","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":25,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 19","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"cf2f2f20e633bfb9bd30a8679fd3a102c10d4b6ae5f7882d3b31d3019ce8d2ce","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore also, as the circle ABCD is to the circle EFGH, so are the cylinders on them which are of equal height."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,ABCD圆也与EFGH圆相同,其高度相等的圆柱体也是如此。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":26,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d41f4fe56dd428c759377c807a93013dffbbe29c7596acfdac57dd182cad51b6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore etc. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,等等,证毕。"}]},{"id":"euclid-12-11.source","contentId":"euclid-12-11","revisionId":"euclid-12-11@raw-65801540c1882cac","order":27,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"7a343d58e88c4a677cbaf30b0a814e49c2a87bed781f8af4c6bb0c0d8b5e10a9","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:12.prop.11/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:12.prop.11\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-12-11:euclid-12-6:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-12-11","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-12-11.construction.3","euclid-12-11.proof.7"],"targetContentId":"euclid-12-6","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:12.prop.11","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:12.prop.11/","sourceLabel":"XII. 6"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-12-11:euclid-10-1:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-12-11","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-12-11.proof.5"],"targetContentId":"euclid-10-1","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:12.prop.11","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:12.prop.11/","sourceLabel":"X. 1"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-12-11:euclid-12-1:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-12-11","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-12-11.proof.6"],"targetContentId":"euclid-12-1","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:12.prop.11","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:12.prop.11/","sourceLabel":"XII. 1"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-12-11:euclid-12-2:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-12-11","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-12-11.proof.6"],"targetContentId":"euclid-12-2","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:12.